bal500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2026, "rank": 133, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2026, "rank": 48, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "americas-most-innovative-companies", "title": "America's Most Innovative Companies", "year": 2026, "rank": 200, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2026, "rank": 43, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2025, "rank": 123, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2025, "rank": 47, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "americas-most-innovative-companies", "title": "America's Most Innovative Companies", "year": 2025, "rank": 132, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2025, "rank": 35, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2024, "rank": 124, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500--transportation", "title": "Fortune Sector Leaders: Transportation", "year": 2024, "rank": 1, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2024, "rank": 45, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2024, "rank": 31, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2023, "rank": 35, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2023, "rank": 101, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "americas-most-innovative-companies", "title": "America's Most Innovative Companies", "year": 2023, "rank": 224, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2023, "rank": 37, "itemDescription": "In 2022 the largest package delivery company in the U.S. saw $100.3 billion in revenue, up 3.1% from the year before. But profits fell 10.4% to $11.5 billion, presaging a difficult 2023. The company has already told investors it expects revenues to be $97 billion for the year, the lower end of its initial guidance, as the pandemic-era e-commerce surge wanes and as inflation inhibits retail spending.<br />\r\n<ul><br />\r\n \t<li>UPS is racing against the clock to negotiate a new labor agreement with the Teamsters union, which represents 340,000 of its workers; its current contract is slated to expire on July 31, 2023.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>In 2022 UPS acquired Italian health care logistics firm Bomi and software company Delivery Service, which makes specialized software for same-day deliveries, as it looks to expand its offerings in both areas.</li><br />\r\n</ul>"}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2022, "rank": 31, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2022, "rank": 97, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2022, "rank": 34, "itemDescription": "<span style=\"font-weight: 400\">UPS increased its revenue 15% in 2021, while profits leaped 860%\u2014despite competition with Amazon, supply-chain setbacks, high consumer expectations, inflation, and a tight labor market all putting pressure on the company. Along the way it sold UPS Freight, part of its trucking infrastructure, to TFI International for $800 million and acquired Roadie, a company that takes advantage of the growing gig economy by matching drivers with deliveries they can complete during other trips they\u2019ve already planned out. UPS was also a central artery for vaccine dispersal in 2021, delivering more than 1.1 billion doses in more than 110 countries.</span>"}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2021, "rank": 28, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2021, "rank": 89, "itemDescription": "Big Brown continues its reign as the leading U.S. delivery business. Pandemic-fueled demand propelled United Parcel Service 40 spots higher, to No. 89, on this year\u2019s Global 500. UPS\u2019s revenues rose 14.2%, to $84.6 billion, in 2020, keeping it ahead of perennial rival FedEx. But the shift in emphasis to residential over commercial parcels took a 70% bite out of profits, which declined to $1.34 billion. A bigger threat looms, as well. Amazon\u2014a major partner, and rising competitor\u2014is doubling down on a delivery network of its own. How the shipper\u2019s CEO, Carol Tom\u00e9, installed on June 1, 2020, confronts this \u201cfrenemy\u201d may prove to be the defining mark of her tenure."}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2021, "rank": 35, "itemDescription": "Big Brown continues its reign as the leading U.S. delivery business. Pandemic-fueled demand propelled United Parcel Service eight spots higher, to No. 35, on this year\u2019s list. UPS\u2019s revenues rose 14.2%, to $84.6 billion, in 2020, keeping it ahead of perennial rival FedEx. But the shift in emphasis to residential over commercial parcels took a 70% bite out of profits, which declined to $1.34 billion. A bigger threat looms, as well. Amazon\u2014a major partner, and rising competitor\u2014is doubling down on a delivery network of its own. How the shipper\u2019s CEO, Carol Tom\u00e9, installed on June 1, 2020, confronts this \u201cfrenemy\u201d may prove to be the defining mark of her tenure."}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2020, "rank": 33, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2020, "rank": 129, "itemDescription": "Big Brown continued its reign as America\u2019s leading delivery business. UPS's revenues rose 3.1%, to $74.1 billion, in 2019, keeping it ahead of perennial rival FedEx. But another threat looms. While FedEx cut ties with Amazon, UPS has hitched its signature brown wagons to the retailer-rocket ship, relying on it for growth. Still unclear is how that alliance will fare as Amazon doubles down on a delivery network of its own. Though UPS will benefit from increasing demand for store-to-door package service amid the coronavirus pandemic, the shipper's new CEO, Carol Tom\u00e9, will have to keep an eye on what may turn out to be a tricky coopetition arrangement with mighty Amazon."}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2020, "rank": 43, "itemDescription": "Big Brown continued its reign as America\u2019s leading delivery business even as it slipped two spots, to No. 43, on this year\u2019s list. UPS's revenues rose 3.1%, to $74.1 billion, in 2019, keeping it ahead of perennial rival FedEx. But another threat looms. While FedEx cut ties with Amazon, UPS has hitched its signature brown wagons to the retailer-rocket ship, relying on it for growth. Still unclear is how that alliance will fare as Amazon doubles down on a delivery network of its own. Though UPS will benefit from increasing demand for store-to-door package service amid the coronavirus pandemic, the shipper's new CEO, Carol Tom\u00e9, will have to keep an eye on what may turn out to be a tricky coopetition arrangement with mighty Amazon."}, {"slug": "change-the-world", "title": "Change the World", "year": 2020, "rank": 49, "itemDescription": "The world\u2019s package delivery leader is also a leader in the emerging, potentially high-margin delivery-drone field. UPS\u2019s Flight Forward unit is partnering with health care systems and others in North Carolina, Virginia, and Utah to deliver patient samples to labs, prescriptions to patients, and supplies to hospitals. Delivery by drone is up to 10 times as fast as by van, as the unmanned aerial craft fly past traffic jams. And since they don\u2019t choke roadways, drones help reduce CO2 emissions."}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2019, "rank": 33, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2019, "rank": 132, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2019, "rank": 41, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2018, "rank": 33, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2018, "rank": 138, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2018, "rank": 44, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2017, "rank": 35, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2017, "rank": 138, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2017, "rank": 46, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2016, "rank": 33, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2016, "rank": 149, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2016, "rank": 48, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2015, "rank": 34, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2015, "rank": 168, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2015, "rank": 47, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2014, "rank": 32, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2014, "rank": 182, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2014, "rank": 50, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title